.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "OS Assignment" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep
function searches the file associated with
.I fp
for lines containing the string specified by
.IR search_str .
Matching lines are stored in the array pointed to by
.IR matches .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines on success and -1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wordCount (3)
